1:["$","$Le",null,{"guide":{"slug":"choose-plants","number":"01","category":"PLANT SELECTION","title":"Choose plants for your first aquarium","intro":"A plant that suits your aquarium is a better starting point than a photo you love. Work through these questions before making your shortlist.","image":"/mas-aquarium-studio/plants.jpg","alt":"Close-up of a small Anubias plant from Micro Aquatic Shop","takeaway":"Match the plant to your setup, then learn how it needs to be planted.","sections":[{"id":"your-setup","title":"Start with the setup you have","body":"Note your tank dimensions, light model and whether you add CO₂. If you do not know your lighting level, take a photo of the light or its label to the shop. A visual guess is not a reliable plant recommendation."},{"id":"plant-needs","title":"Check each plant’s needs","body":"Look at its light and CO₂ requirements, mature size and planting method. Tropica’s Easy category is a useful starting point for less demanding choices. Still check the individual species against your tank.","items":["Leave room for the plant’s mature height and spread.","Check whether it roots in the substrate, attaches to a surface or floats.","Consider the needs of any fish already in the aquarium."]},{"id":"planting-method","title":"Plan where it will grow","body":"Anubias and Java fern have a rhizome: the thick stem from which roots and leaves grow. Keep this stem above the substrate. For rooted or stem plants, follow the instructions for that plant."},{"id":"shortlist","title":"Bring a useful shortlist","body":"Save the plants you like and bring your setup details. Ask the shop to help you compare suitable options before you order."}],"questions":["Does this plant suit my light and CO₂ setup?","How large will it grow?","How should I plant it?"],"sources":[{"title":"Tropica — Plant care FAQ","url":"https://tropica.com/en/guide/faq/"},{"title":"Tropica — Planting","url":"https://tropica.com/en/guide/get-the-right-start/planting/"}],"next":"help-new-plants-settle","shopPlants":true}}]
